# Netlify routing. First matching rule wins, and a rule is only consulted when no
# static file matches the request — so the prerendered public pages written by
# scripts/prerender.mjs (dist/<route>/index.html) are served directly and never
# reach these rules.
#
# What is left for the rules to decide:
#
#   1. Private application surfaces -> the SPA shell, 200. They are client-routed
#      and guarded by ProtectedRoute / PlatformAdminRoute / PlatformOwnerRoute, so
#      the shell must still be served for deep links and page reloads.
#
#      The target is /app-shell.html, NOT /index.html: index.html is now the
#      prerendered HOMEPAGE, so falling back to it would serve marketing markup
#      (with the homepage canonical and an indexable robots tag) on the customer
#      portal and then discard it all on hydration. /app-shell.html is the
#      untouched client template with an empty #root, marked noindex.
#
#      Both the exact prefix root AND its deep paths are listed: on Netlify
#      "/app/*" does NOT match "/app", and relying on the splat alone would 404
#      every portal root. Server-level noindex for these lives in public/_headers.
#
#   2. Everything else -> a real 404. Previously "/* /index.html 200" answered
#      every unknown URL with the homepage shell at HTTP 200, which turned the
#      entire unknown URL space into a soft 404.

/app                /app-shell.html   200
/app/*              /app-shell.html   200
/admin              /app-shell.html   200
/admin/*            /app-shell.html   200
/owner              /app-shell.html   200
/owner/*            /app-shell.html   200
/auth               /app-shell.html   200
/auth/*             /app-shell.html   200
/d                  /app-shell.html   200
/d/*                /app-shell.html   200

/*                  /404.html         404
